Recompiler: "register locals" code generation (PS2X_CODEGEN=locals while running ps2_recomp; the pipeline sets it by
default, build.cmd -Codegen classic leaves it off). Without it the generated code is byte for byte the same. Adapted from the Killzone
port's patch 0017 (drakolordx7/KillzoneRecomp) to this runtime: a generated function keeps the guest GPRs it uses in C++
locals (host registers) and stores ctx->pc only where it can be read (calls into the runtime, the instruction before a
branch). Every statement that hands ctx to other code (calls, returns, syscalls, stubs, exceptions, helpers taking ctx)
stays classic between PS2_FLUSH() (locals -> ctx) and PS2_RELOAD(); the loop checkpoint writes the registers back only
when the full checkpoint runs (PS2Runtime::eeCheckpointQuiet / eeCheckpointFull). A function the rewrite cannot place is
emitted classic as a whole (600 of 6,415 in God of War). PS2X_CODEGEN_FUNCS=<file> restricts it to listed functions.
The Killzone dispatch changes (direct calls, tail-jump following, its patch 0023) are not included: this runtime's call
return protocol (checkpoint / jump serials in dispatchGuestBranch) differs.
Measured on the ship (Xeon E5-2666 v3, RX 580, 2x, with 01-07): EE thread 3.0-3.4 -> 2.3-2.6 s busy per 5 s in combat
(about -22 %); 55-60 fps in both (the VU1 worker is the limit); boot, gameplay and image as before; 586k -> 366k
ctx->pc stores in the generated code.

